<div class="docs-sdk-page">

    <div class="docs-eyebrow">MODDING SDK / REAL CONTRACTS</div>

    <h1>
        The Crafty <span class="docs-accent">SDK</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        The SDK is a separate .NET 10 project with public contracts.
        This page describes what the checked-in interfaces actually
        expose today—and what they do not.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-warning">
        <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle"></i>

        <div>
            <strong>Important: the SDK surface is not the same as a complete mod loader</strong>

            <p>
                <code>IMod</code> and content registry interfaces exist.
                However, the game currently initializes its built-in MainMod
                directly; there is no external assembly discovery/loading
                pipeline in the checked-in code, and <code>Crafty.MDK</code>
                is an empty placeholder.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Project characteristics</h2>

    <p>
        <code>Crafty.SDK.csproj</code> targets <code>net10.0</code>,
        enables nullable reference types and implicit usings, uses the
        latest language version, and allows unsafe blocks. The SDK
        project itself has no project references.
    </p>

    <h2>Mod entry point: IMod</h2>

    <p>
        The interface is in namespace <code>Crafty.SDK</code> and
        requires these members:
    </p>

    <div class="docs-code-card">
        <div class="docs-code-title">
            <span>Crafty.SDK.IMod.cs</span>
            <span>ACTUAL INTERFACE SHAPE</span>
        </div>

        <pre><code>
public interface IMod
{
    string Id { get; }
    string Name { get; }
    string Version { get; }
    string AssetsDirectory { get; }

    void Initilaize(IModContext context);
}
</code></pre>
    </div>

    <p>
        The method is spelled <code>Initilaize</code> in the source.
        Implement that exact spelling when implementing this snapshot's
        interface.
    </p>

    <h2>Mod context</h2>

    <p>
        <code>IModContext</code> currently exposes only three services:
    </p>

    <ul class="docs-list">
        <li>
            <code>ILogger Logger</code> — logging through
            <code>Log(string message)</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>IBlockRegistry Blocks</code> — block registration and lookup.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>IItemRegistry Items</code> — item registration and lookup.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        It does not currently expose a world instance, player service,
        event bus, UI registration service, input API, renderer, or
        general dependency injection container.
    </p>

